# Docs / planning / agent tooling — not needed in the build context (cuts context bloat).
#
# `research/` and `roadmap/` were removed from this list (RM-38 WP 3.3): both trees ceased to exist
# when the planning bundle was consolidated under `planning/`, so the two entries had been matching
# nothing for months while the 30 MB tree that replaced them was shipped in full.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EXCLUDING `planning/` OUTRIGHT — it is a BUILD-CONTEXT DEPENDENCY, not docs.
# The build stage runs `pnpm build`, whose first step is `pnpm docs:bundle`
# (`scripts/build-docs-bundle.mjs`), and that script reads `planning/user-guide/DC-*` to generate
# `apps/web/public/doc-content/` — the in-app manual. It refuses to emit an empty bundle, so a
# blanket `planning/` exclusion does not degrade the image, it FAILS the build. Measured, not
# reasoned: a probe image built from a context with a blanket `planning/` exclusion sees
# `planning_files=0` and dies with
# `Error: build-docs-bundle: user guide directory not found: /app/planning/user-guide`;
# the same probe against the rules below finds the guide and completes.
#
# So the exclusion is the bundle MINUS the one subtree the build reads. `planning/**` catches every
# future subtree by default (a new one is excluded automatically rather than silently re-inflating
# the context), and the negation re-admits exactly the guide. Nothing else in the build reads
# `planning/` — `build-docs-bundle.mjs` opens `planning/user-guide` and `CHANGELOG.md` and nothing
# else, and the only other references to the path in the workspace are vitest tests, which do not
# run in the image build.
planning/**
!planning/user-guide/**
docs/
.claude/
.github/
